# Refactoring and keeping rules in sync

When a refactor changes how something should be done (naming, layers, schema, localization, tests):

1. Read the matching files in `.cursor/rules/` (`implementation-rules-index`).
2. Update a rule when the refactor replaces an old convention.
3. Add one new rule when the pattern should be repeated and is not documented yet.
4. Add a row to `implementation-rules-index` when you add a rule.

Do this for convention changes, not for a one-off bugfix.
